{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation","id":1178883,"title":"Victorian Mage: speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T11:42:53-08:00","id":1178883,"title":"Victorian Mage: speculation","content":"OK: what do we know about what's going to be in the upcoming <b>Victorian Age: Mage</b>? What do we hope will be in there?<br /> <br /> We know that the Victorian Age is when the remnants of the Order of Reason reforged themselves as the Technocracy; so we're going to be seeing the Technocracy 1.0. The Union will include the Electrodyne Engineers and the Difference Engineers, the predecessors of the modern Etherites and VAs respectively; and the timeframe covered by this age ends before (or perhaps as?) the Electrodyne Engineers jump ship and the Union undergoes its first reorganization. <br /> <br /> This is also the era where the Hollow Ones got their start, though they weren't called the Hollow Ones (or even widely recognized as a group) at the time. The Batini were still among the Traditions, but otherwise the Traditions were more or less the same as they were nearly a century later. <br /> <br /> I know that a previous plan for VA:M was going to tinker around with the magic system, giving each Tradition a Minor Sphere of its own; but I will be shocked if something like this makes it into this newest version. More likely, we'll see discussions about how Focus differs between the Victorian and contemporary ages, with a mention of what Paradigms were prevalent in the Victorian Age, how Practices differed, and what Instruments were available. Also a bit of a discussion about where the line between Vulgar and Coincidental lies, as mundane technology was still nowhere near as capable as it is today.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:55:30-08:00","id":1178925,"title":"","content":"My hope is that this book takes the giant toolkit of M20 and selects only what is needed for someone to run a game out of a relatively small book. <br /> <br /> Regarding the setting, it's a great time for Ascension. Colonialism is in full swing world-wide and it'll be interesting to see what stances the council of nine takes regarding imperialism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:32:54-08:00","id":1178973,"title":"","content":"I'd like them to reexamine Secret Societies, like they did with Victorian Age Vampire, but from the perspective of mages. Finally explain - or give possible explanations for - the Golden Dawn's place in the World of Darkness, when there's already a centuries-old Hermetic conspiracy. VAV had nothing to say about the Order of Hermes, since it was a Vampire book. So more Mage-centric material would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:58:13-08:00","id":1178983,"title":"","content":"I bet you anything London\u2019s going to be the focal point for all things Technocratic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:04:23-08:00","id":1178986,"title":"","content":"It's really important to me that we see the full degree that by rising in this era the Union is built on a foundation of eugenics and imperialism.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the increased factionalization of the Traditions into mystic societies without strong cohesive identity might be strongly attributed to conflict over imperialism between the European Trads and the rest - especially if the Society of the Black Willow and the Acharne control the Euthanatos and Ecstatic seats respectively - to the outrage of the Chakravanti and Sahajiya, who of course are invested in and badly scarred by the &quot;Mutiny&quot; of 1857.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:48:16-08:00","id":1179235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation#post1178883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK: what do we know about what's going to be in the upcoming <b>Victorian Age: Mage</b>? What do we hope will be in there?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they will not focus on London and the United Kingdom except when it is pertinent and feels like the correct approach.<br /> The existence of a mundane human nation which has a high level of power and influence during this period is not at all relevant in regards to the lives and matters of the vast majority of True Mages and of other Nightfolk; and has small to none relevancy in regards to vast majority of actions of individual Mages and Mage factions and groups.<br /> <br /> For example I'd like to read about how early Technocracy Amalgams acted and worked all over Europe - including Eastern Europe and Scandinavia - and the South America and the North America.<br /> Were there any meaningful and interesting differences depending on where they were located; and how much did the location impact the transitions and changes that happened to Fellowships / Amalgams as the Technocratic Union was established and developed as an organization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-25-2018, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T12:01:14-08:00","id":1179276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1179235#post1179235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they will not focus on London and the United Kingdom except when it is pertinent and feels like the correct approach.<br /> The existence of a mundane human nation which has a high level of power and influence during this period is not at all relevant in regards to the lives and matters of the vast majority of True Mages and of other Nightfolk;</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaactually. The transformation of the Order Of Reason into the Technocracy in Queen Victoria's age was, well, built on the back and bastion that was the globe-spanning British Commonwealth. With support of Queen Victoria herself.<br /> So yeah, we'll definitely get a good focus on London and Britain, and all its arms around the world at that time.<br /> Not that I'd not want the book to cover as much ground space as possible all over the map, but purely from a Mage-history standpoint, Britain and London had a HUGE effect on the life of True Mages at the time. One that lasts to this very day. The Technocratic Union itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-25-2018, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T12:51:10-08:00","id":1179286,"title":"","content":"It would seem a hugely missed opportunity not to explore what\u2019s going on in the Imperial colonies as a central focus. India in particular has a rich setting for the era and major conflicts that tie in well with the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Were it up to me, i\u2019d put focus on the British Empire as a whole, rather than just London or GB, but treat events and settings outside the Empire as more marginal - but if the book did well enough, do supplements on things like Japanese Civil War and Meiji Restoration as a setting, or the American West (with required Werewolf/Umbra Storm crossover info).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T20:34:04-08:00","id":1179421,"title":"","content":"It's the Victorian Age. Obviously they're going to center a lot of it on London and the British Empire.<br /> <br /> It also allows for killer crossover games since Victorian Age Vampire had a similar focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T21:05:33-07:00","id":1194727,"title":"","content":"I just noticed it\u2019s now appeared at the first draft phase on the Monday meeting notes.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s happening!<br /> <br /> Come on: Eugenicist Social Darwinist portrayal of the birth of the Union!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T21:41:26-07:00","id":1194734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1194727#post1194727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed it\u2019s now appeared at the first draft phase on the Monday meeting notes.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s happening!<br /> <br /> Come on: Eugenicist Social Darwinist portrayal of the birth of the Union!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehm. Hate to burst your bubble, but it's been at First Drafts for awhile now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T21:52:20-07:00","id":1194737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1194734#post1194734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehm. Hate to burst your bubble, but it's been at First Drafts for awhile now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well I hadn\u2019t noticed so still pleasant news for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T00:36:58-07:00","id":1314475,"title":"","content":"Are the Lodges from the old outline going to factor in, do you think? I adored everything in that draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T02:42:00-07:00","id":1314488,"title":"","content":"I just hope the wrongness of colonialism is contained a side bar and not 70% of the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:01:57-07:00","id":1314500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314488#post1314488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope the wrongness of colonialism is contained a side bar and not 70% of the book</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it\u2019s a historical era defined by it. Not sure what you want here when like, India, China, Egypt, and many others\u2019 situations in this time period exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:20:06-07:00","id":1314508,"title":"","content":"I can understand the desire for the book not to become a lecture, which is what Dwight's \u201c70%\u201d figure was trying to convey. But yeah; it <i>is</i> a defining feature of the Victorian Age, and in particular the newly-founded Technocracy; so I don't see it being confined to a single side bar either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T16:24:52-07:00","id":1314604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314508#post1314508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand the desire for the book not to become a lecture, which is what Dwight's \u201c70%\u201d figure was trying to convey. But yeah; it <i>is</i> a defining feature of the Victorian Age, and in particular the newly-founded Technocracy; so I don't see it being confined to a single side bar either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IF its only set in England rather like what the intial outline seemed to indicate vs &quot;any place in the 19th century&quot; you might reduce down to... 40 percent!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T17:14:38-07:00","id":1314609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314604#post1314604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> IF its only set in England rather like what the intial outline seemed to indicate vs &amp;quot;any place in the 19th century&amp;quot; you might reduce down to... 40 percent!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, like... Great Britain in the time period is booming because of colonialism, though. That\u2019s why they\u2019re wealthy, that\u2019s most of what we characterize this as a time period by. I feel like there\u2019s no real way to describe the setting that does\u2019t read like \u201ccolonialism bad\u201d other than by pretending the actions of empire don\u2019t exist, and that\u2019s not a book I think is worth buying. If we have Chakravanti, Akashics, and Dreamspeakers in this setting, then we have the colonialism that\u2019s brought them into the British sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T17:26:20-07:00","id":1314610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314609#post1314609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, like... Great Britain in the time period is booming because of colonialism, though. That\u2019s why they\u2019re wealthy, that\u2019s most of what we characterize this as a time period by. I feel like there\u2019s no real way to describe the setting that does\u2019t read like \u201ccolonialism bad\u201d other than by pretending the actions of empire don\u2019t exist, and that\u2019s not a book I think is worth buying. If we have Chakravanti, Akashics, and Dreamspeakers in this setting, then we have the colonialism that\u2019s brought them into the British sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The earlier outline seemed to not indicate any of those groups would be available(With Dreamspeakers perhaps being NPCs) with the main focus being Lodges in England that were sort of Tier 2 Hermetic/Verbena/Order of REason. Where each group would have theirown lesser spheres and not have a complete set. Now this would still be heavily effected by Colonialism(see the 40 percent) but it wouldn't be the same as a game that was intended to have you duking it out in the middle of the Opium wars or the Mutiny or the Zulu wars(which would I think be 70 percent or more..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T17:33:50-07:00","id":1314612,"title":"","content":"What is this \u201cearlier outline\u201d you're referring to? If it's what I'm thinking of, it was conceived decades ago during the Mage Revised years and isn't a factor in the upcoming book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T17:40:51-07:00","id":1314614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314612#post1314612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this \u201cearlier outline\u201d you're referring to? If it's what I'm thinking of, it was conceived decades ago during the Mage Revised years and isn't a factor in the upcoming book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be the one. I mean it honestly could be ignored. just saying a game set in Lodges in England proper is going to be LESS focused on Colonialism than say one where &quot;play out the Secret Magical founding of Hong Kong&quot; is an intended play style. I still think there would be a huge percentage in the England game, just not as huge a percentage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T22:58:06-07:00","id":1314657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314614#post1314614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be the one. I mean it honestly could be ignored. just saying a game set in Lodges in England proper is going to be LESS focused on Colonialism than say one where &quot;play out the Secret Magical founding of Hong Kong&quot; is an intended play style. I still think there would be a huge percentage in the England game, just not as huge a percentage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually liked that set up quite a bit and have been using a slightly modified version of it for my own Victorian games for the past decade or so. (Also worked pretty well for 18th century games, I found.) The lodges I ended up using were pretty diverse and a lot of fun. Especially when I started find real world inspired ways to incorporate Dreamspeakers, Batini, and the like into period European mysticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T00:57:46-07:00","id":1315113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1179286#post1179286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would seem a hugely missed opportunity not to explore what\u2019s going on in the Imperial colonies as a central focus. India in particular has a rich setting for the era and major conflicts that tie in well with the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, don't forget Germany, and its new empire building, or the gradual collapse of the Ottoman Empire, or the scramble for African and even Pacific territories by the imperial powers. There is more to the world than London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T10:27:10-07:00","id":1315212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315113#post1315113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, don't forget Germany, and its new empire building, or the gradual collapse of the Ottoman Empire, or the scramble for African and even Pacific territories by the imperial powers. There is more to the world than London.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, though given the associations inherent in the word \u201cVictorian\u201d, I do expect the British Empire to take primary focus (afterall if the whole world got even attention this would be just as much a \u201cWild West\u201d setting as \u201cVictorian\u201d given that those are contemporary eras, and they\u2019re obviously not giving that the same attention... could be a cool supplement though). I just hope they take a balanced look at the empire as a whole rather than treat everything not on the home island as a bit of an afterthought (*coughs in Victorian Age Vampire\u2019s direction*).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-29-2019, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T10:42:17-07:00","id":1315217,"title":"","content":"If they want to make it a world-spanning supplement that includes 19th century Germany, the Ottoman Empire, or, yes, the American West, \u201cVictorian Age\u201d would still be a better name for it than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T11:07:20-07:00","id":1315227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315217#post1315217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they want to make it a world-spanning supplement that includes 19th century Germany, the Ottoman Empire, or, yes, the American West, \u201cVictorian Age\u201d would still be a better name for it than most.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a creative exercise, I once did an outline for &quot;Mage: Victorian Twilight&quot; as the game's '98 historical line (following The Dark Ages and Savage Rome). One of the very early sourcebooks was <i>The Grand Tour</i>, which ideally would've looked at its different areas from both native and outsider perspectives. Chapters being the British Empire, the Continent (and their holdings), the Americas, the Orient (in this case the Ottomans, Siam, Japan, Ethiopia, and anywhere else still independent), and Ends of the Earth (mythic places, the poles, the moon, the Hollow Earth, etc.). Also London by Twilight (the signature city), and later Transylvania by Twilight (Vampire crossover), Sunset Empires (the Far East), Arabian Twilight, India: Jewel of the Empire, an African book I could never decide on a title for, WoD: The Wild West, and a book about space and umbral travel. All the regional books would've included new lodges from those places and cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T14:11:55-07:00","id":1315266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315217#post1315217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they want to make it a world-spanning supplement that includes 19th century Germany, the Ottoman Empire, or, yes, the American West, \u201cVictorian Age\u201d would still be a better name for it than most.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it\u2019s late 19th Century, rather than mid, I\u2019d suggest \u201cGilded Age\u201d if it isn\u2019t British Empire focused.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s mid-19th Century, play up the American Civil War and the Meiji Restoration against the Daedalus vs Technocrat conflict while the Trads are falling apart over colonialism, and call it \u201cBrother vs Brother\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T14:18:54-07:00","id":1315268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1314488#post1314488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope the wrongness of colonialism is contained a side bar and not 70% of the book</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not making it a central theme of the setting would be the moral equivalent of making slavery a sidebar in a book on the American Civil War. It\u2019s the cornerstone the entire society is built on.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that a game that puts its primary focus on Occult secret societies and their mysteries is better suited for Awakening than Ascension. Ascension is ABOUT cultural paradigmatic conflict and imperial authority imposing its paradigm on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-29-2019, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T14:28:44-07:00","id":1315272,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, anyone have any inspirational material that strongly influences their take on the period? I'm a big fan of Anne Perry's mystery novels, both the William Monk series set in the 50s and 60s, and the Thomas and Charlotte Pitt one set in the 80s and 90s. Also GURPS Steampunk and the Comme il Faut book from Castle Falkenstein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T14:52:46-07:00","id":1315278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315272#post1315272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, anyone have any inspirational material that strongly influences their take on the period? I'm a big fan of Anne Perry's mystery novels, both the William Monk series set in the 50s and 60s, and the Thomas and Charlotte Pitt one set in the 80s and 90s. Also GURPS Steampunk and the Comme il Faut book from Castle Falkenstein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only ever saw the first season, but I adored Ripper Street, a period police procedural set in Whitechapel with very nice production values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T16:44:31-07:00","id":1315293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315272#post1315272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, anyone have any inspirational material that strongly influences their take on the period? I'm a big fan of Anne Perry's mystery novels, both the William Monk series set in the 50s and 60s, and the Thomas and Charlotte Pitt one set in the 80s and 90s. Also GURPS Steampunk and the Comme il Faut book from Castle Falkenstein.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Penny Dreadful, except the second half of the last season.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T16:55:55-07:00","id":1315299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315293#post1315293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say Penny Dreadful, except the second half of the last season.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched the first season of it on Netfix a couple of years ago and couldn't get into it for some reason. Not that I found it bad or anything (and I really love Timothy Dalton as an actor), but it just didn't click with me. I'm not sure why. The sets and costumes were lovely thou.<br /> <br /> I need to get around to watching Ripper Street at some point.<br /> <br /> And I recommend Alan Moore's From Hell graphic novel. The movie version barely scratched the surface of what was in the original. The occult tour of London is a real gem, especially the footnotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T21:02:50-07:00","id":1315370,"title":"","content":"The Frankenstein Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T15:27:02-07:00","id":1315953,"title":"","content":"&quot;The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen&quot; graphic novel. But I don't expect Mage to be quite as pulpy. <br /> On the more subdued end of the spectrum I really enjoyed two series with an 1890s setting; The Alienist and the Lizzie Borden Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T18:44:11-07:00","id":1316350,"title":"","content":"I've read The Alienist novel and it's sequel, but haven't seen the series yet. Both are a really good look at turn of the century New York City. I also recommend Michael Crichton's The Great Train Robbery and the film version he directed with Sean Connery and Donald Sutherland. <br /> <br /> Over the years, I've found Cthulhu by Gaslight to be fairly useful. I've been trying for years, still unsuccessfully, to find a hardcopy of the Golden Dawn sourcebook Pagan Publishing put out in 96 for a reasonable price. Someday it <i>will</i> be mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T23:09:58-07:00","id":1316379,"title":"","content":"Of you want to read something a little less fictional there is Dirty Old London: The Victorian Fight Against Filth by Lee Jackson. It covers the creation of the sewage system, street cleaning, public toilets, baths, the cemetery reform movement and the chimney sweeps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T03:11:52-07:00","id":1316789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315953#post1315953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen&quot; graphic novel. But I don't expect Mage to be quite as pulpy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Mage includes the Society of Ether as a primary group. They're so pulpy, I'm surprised their Trad Books haven't disintegrated by now.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Etherites have a huge emphasis on Two-Fisted adventure. Other groups can be bent towards pulp archetypes, even as early as the Victorian era. It depends on how you want to flavor characters, and what tone the Storyteller is going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T08:47:41-07:00","id":1316836,"title":"","content":"While true, bear in mind that at the time of the actual Victorian Age, the Sons of Ether didn't exist yet. They were the Electrodyne Engineers, one of the founding Conventions of the Technocracy. Which, incidentally, is one of the reasons I hope (and suspect) that Victorian Mage won't fall into the trap of presenting the Technocracy solely through the lens of being \u201cevil colonialists\u201d. <br /> <br /> Another is the Analytic Reckoners: while they admittedly have a way to go before they discover the Digital Web and become the Virtual Adepts, the rather libertine attitudes of the VAs didn't just spring up out of nowhere. Especially with the Analytic Reckoners, there's a lot of potential for Steampunk goodness in the setting. <br /> <br /> (Ironically, the Electrodyne Engineers aren't so much interested in \u201csteampunk\u201d as they are in the potential inherent in electricity. That said, they're primarily heirs to the Solificati and champions of the Book of Ether, which promotes a philosophy that the new Technocracy has not yet rejected \u2014<br /> though admittedly it hasn't embraced it, either.)<br /> <br /> (Conversely, the Batini are still among the Traditions at this point; and Mount Qaf is still a thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-04-2019, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T15:16:30-07:00","id":1316897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1315953#post1315953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen&quot; graphic novel. But I don't expect Mage to be quite as pulpy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If asked to come up with an Ecstatic signature character for the period, I'd be hard pressed to top the real life Sir Richard Francis Burton. The man's life reads like a pulp adventure serial, and then he decided to devote his retirement years to translating, publishing, and founding societies devoted to Asian erotica. And that's just what we know, as his wife apparently burned most of his journals after he died. The man could just as well visited Shambala, Irem, Atlantis, and Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T15:24:03-07:00","id":1317063,"title":"","content":"Speaking of pulp, The Hollow Earth is very much a thing in Victorian literature. Underground seas the size of Europe, artificial suns, various lost/aliens/master races, and multiple feminist utopias are all part of period literature on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T04:03:37-07:00","id":1317153,"title":"","content":"Do we have any word on the magic system that this book will use? WIll it be the spheres, the Pillars from dark ages mage, or some combination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T08:57:26-07:00","id":1317191,"title":"","content":"They haven't said; but Sorcerer's Crusade used the Spheres, and this is set centuries later. As well, Phil is writing it, and has expressed no interest in doing anything other than the Spheres. I'll be shocked if it's anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T06:25:26-07:00","id":1317785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1317191#post1317191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They haven't said; but Sorcerer's Crusade used the Spheres, and this is set centuries later. As well, Phil is writing it, and has expressed no interest in doing anything other than the Spheres. I'll be shocked if it's anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, keep in mind that sorcerer's crusade was written way before dark ages mage and the pillar system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T07:52:00-07:00","id":1317807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1317785#post1317785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, keep in mind that sorcerer's crusade was written way before dark ages mage and the pillar system</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; and it was written by Phil Brucato, who wasn't around when Dark Ages Mage and the pillar system were written. My impression (though I admittedly don't have anything to support this) is that he's not much of a fan of the latter; and now that he's back in charge of Mage, he's more likely to stick with the notion that \u201cthe Sorcerers Crusade established the Spheres in the Mage community, and they've been used by everyone ever since\u201d. <br /> <br /> Note also that the original treatment of Victorian Mage (which was going to give each Tradition a Minor Sphere) was written during the MRev era, after Brucato had left. I don't think Phil is interested in going even that far, let alone all the way into a Victorian-era Foundation and Pillars system. <br /> <br /> Note that this has nothing to do with my own views on the subject. Personally, I've been a fan of using the Disparates as a vehicle for a modern-day Foundation-and-Pillars system (on the basis that the Disparates, by definition, never accepted what the Traditions were offering) and of giving each Tradition a \u201cvariant Sphere\u201d (usually, but not always, the Sphere that a given Tradition is associated with in the Council of Nine) to represent that Tradition's special insights into that area of magick. But that's all a matter of how I'd like to see things done, not how I expect that they will be done. <br /> <br /> As things stand, I think that any sort of Foundation and Pillars system in any context other than Dark Ages Mage will be restricted to fringe areas such as V20's Black Hand supplement or Storyteller's Vault products; I don't expect to see them anywhere in the M20 publishing line. As well, I think that Sphere variants will be restricted to the three Technocratic variants (Data, Dimensional Science, and Primal Utility) that appeared in M20, and that even they are going to firmly remain in the \u201coptional rules\u201d territory. <br /> <br /> And with the possible exception of Primal Utility, I don't expect to see any of them make even that much of an appearance in Victorian Mage: as I see it, the emergence of Dimensional Science is closely correlated with the Void Engineers' introduction of Tychoidean Cosmology and the departure of the Electrodyne Engineers from the Technocracy (in Victorian Mage, I expect that the notion of the Ether will be broadly accepted by those in the Union who care about such things), and the Data variant will have to wait at least until Alan Turing and the discovery of the Digital Web nearly a century later. <br /> <br /> Conversely, I tend to link the emergence of Primal Utility to Adam Smith's \u201cthe Wealth of Nations\u201d, which precedes the Victorian Age by almost a century; so I could see the fledgeling Invisible Exchequer featuring that variant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T15:39:12-07:00","id":1317892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1316897#post1316897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If asked to come up with an Ecstatic signature character for the period, I'd be hard pressed to top the real life Sir Richard Francis Burton. The man's life reads like a pulp adventure serial, and then he decided to devote his retirement years to translating, publishing, and founding societies devoted to Asian erotica. And that's just what we know, as his wife apparently burned most of his journals after he died. The man could just as well visited Shambala, Irem, Atlantis, and Mars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean Barsoom? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T22:20:44-07:00","id":1317971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178883-victorian-mage-speculation?p=1317892#post1317892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you mean Barsoom? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Somewhere in my collection of gaming sourcebook miscellanea, I have the Space 1889 guide to the planets which includes period ideas of what Mars, Venus, and Mercury are like. I find it useful for period games involving that sort of thing. Also for modern games where Mages might visit what I call the Bygone versions of those worlds.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i